{"id": "building-inspection-favours", "title": "Building permits for sale: the inspector, the engineer and the plan checkers", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.175, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "371170fd8b5b66ff", "words": 376, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "San Francisco’s building department checks plans, and signs off finished work.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.17, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Department of Building Inspection", "sub": "checks plans, signs off finished work"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.83, 1.14, 1.58, 1.9, 2.46, 2.67, 3.11, 3.33, 3.68]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[2]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "Federal charges say one design firm paid senior inspector Bernard Curran for each inspection. How much?", "t0": 4.29, "t1": 10.35, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The price of a sign-off", "sub": "charged: paid to senior inspector Bernard Curran"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.76, 1.02, 1.22, 1.62, 1.9, 2.17, 2.5, 2.98, 3.37, 3.77, 3.95, 4.16, 5.37, 5.6]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[2]", "links[5]"], "text": "1,500 dollars.", "t0": 10.35, "t1": 12.03, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1,500", "label": "per inspection, to Curran"}, "emph": ["1,500"], "wt": [0.04, 0.26, 0.64, 0.89, 1.15]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["defense[0]", "status", "links[5]"], "text": "The Real Deal reported that two executives admitted it. All eight charged federally pleaded guilty.", "t0": 12.55, "t1": 18.06, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Eight guilty pleas", "sub": "eight charged federally; The Real Deal: two admitted the $1,500"}, "emph": ["pleaded guilty"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.35, 0.6, 0.96, 1.12, 1.32, 1.93, 2.35, 3.17, 3.48, 3.72, 4.16, 4.63, 5.0]}, {"scene": "char", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]"], "text": "Next, engineer Rodrigo Santos, once president of the Building Inspection Commission.", "t0": 18.28, "t1": 22.53, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Rodrigo Santos", "kicker": "The engineer", "sub": "former president, Building Inspection Commission"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 1.02, 1.46, 2.08, 2.37, 2.72, 2.8, 2.88, 3.2, 3.72]}, {"scene": "char", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "His 13 clients wrote checks to a sports nonprofit Curran coached for. 9,600 dollars.", "t0": 22.65, "t1": 28.72, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Santos’s clients", "sub": "13 checks, $9,600"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Athletic nonprofit", "sub": "Curran coached for it"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Bernard Curran", "sub": "senior building inspector"}], "kicker": "May 2017 to April 2019"}, "emph": ["9,600"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.65, 1.12, 1.34, 1.66, 1.8, 1.86, 2.23, 2.82, 3.12, 3.45, 4.3, 4.6, 5.03, 5.27, 5.56]}, {"scene": "char", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Why a charity? So the money never reached Curran, and it looked like giving.", "t0": 28.84, "t1": 32.86, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Santos’s clients", "sub": "13 checks, $9,600"}, {"art": "money", "name": "Athletic nonprofit", "sub": "Curran coached for it"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Bernard Curran", "sub": "senior building inspector"}], "kicker": "May 2017 to April 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.34, 1.42, 1.6, 1.7, 1.95, 2.2, 2.53, 2.99, 3.17, 3.23, 3.42, 3.6]}, {"scene": "char", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[1]", "links[3]"], "text": "But all 13 donors got a sign-off from him.", "t0": 32.98, "t1": 35.27, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "13", "label": "donors who got official action from Curran"}, "emph": ["13"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.35, 0.78, 1.16, 1.33, 1.39, 1.83, 2.04]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "In 2017, a developer whose projects Curran inspected lent him money for his mortgage. How much?", "t0": 35.49, "t1": 41.1, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "His mortgage", "kicker": "The loan", "sub": "March 2017"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 0.93, 1.0, 1.43, 1.64, 2.18, 2.47, 2.98, 3.22, 3.36, 3.61, 3.78, 3.92, 4.95, 5.17]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "260,000 dollars.", "t0": 41.1, "t1": 42.76, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$260,000", "label": "from a developer he inspected"}, "emph": ["260,000"], "wt": [0.04, 0.25, 0.5, 0.82, 1.16]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why", "suspicious[2].what", "established[14]"], "text": "30,000 was never paid back. So that forgiven debt counts as a payment.", "t0": 43.28, "t1": 47.75, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["repaid", "most of it"], "b": ["never repaid", "$30,000"]}, "emph": ["payment"], "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.69, 0.84, 1.08, 1.33, 2.26, 2.46, 2.65, 3.07, 3.38, 3.73, 3.87, 3.92]}, {"scene": "loan", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "In 2021, he told the City Attorney a relative had lent it. That was false.", "t0": 47.87, "t1": 52.29, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the loan came from a relative"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.41, 0.98, 1.1, 1.32, 1.42, 1.66, 2.05, 2.13, 2.52, 2.66, 2.92, 3.54, 3.79, 3.93]}, {"scene": "sia", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[2]", "established[6]"], "text": "That design firm was SIA Consulting. Its executives, like Siavash Tahbazof, paid plan checkers too.", "t0": 52.51, "t1": 58.71, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "SIA Consulting", "kicker": "The plan checkers", "sub": "Siavash Tahbazof, Reza Khoshnevisan, Bahman Ghassemzadeh"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.62, 0.87, 1.07, 1.63, 2.74, 2.95, 3.58, 3.78, 4.3, 4.88, 5.13, 5.43, 5.84]}, {"scene": "sia", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[7]", "established[8]"], "text": "Rudy Pada, from 2003. Then Cyril Yu, until 2021.", "t0": 58.83, "t1": 63.0, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Rudy Pada", "2003 to 2017"], "b": ["Cyril Yu", "2018 to 2021"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.73, 0.93, 1.1, 1.46, 2.19, 2.46, 2.82, 3.06, 3.32, 3.6]}, {"scene": "sia", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[7]", "links[6]"], "text": "Cash, meals, drinks, and for Pada, an 85,000 dollar loan with no interest.", "t0": 63.12, "t1": 68.31, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Cash, meals, drinks", "kicker": "The plan checkers", "sub": "and an interest-free loan to Pada", "chip": "$85,000"}, "emph": ["85,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 1.04, 1.5, 1.69, 1.84, 2.64, 2.83, 3.37, 3.7, 4.0, 4.24, 4.44, 4.62]}, {"scene": "sia", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "It ran 18 years, a year past the City Hall scandal of January 2020.", "t0": 68.43, "t1": 72.73, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "18 years", "kicker": "The plan checkers", "sub": "and a year past January 2020"}, "emph": ["18 years"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.44, 0.87, 1.3, 1.44, 1.68, 1.96, 2.06, 2.3, 2.51, 2.97, 3.1, 3.59, 3.9]}, {"scene": "checks", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Santos also kept his clients’ checks for City permit fees.", "t0": 72.95, "t1": 76.09, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "RoDBIgo SANTOS"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.56, 0.87, 1.08, 1.18, 1.59, 1.94, 2.11, 2.37, 2.7]}, {"scene": "checks", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "He changed one, made out to DBI, to spell his own name.", "t0": 76.21, "t1": 78.85, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "RoDBIgo SANTOS"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.49, 0.77, 0.97, 1.11, 1.2, 1.69, 1.78, 2.03, 2.13, 2.29]}, {"scene": "checks", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "About 445 checks, from 2012 to 2019. How much?", "t0": 78.97, "t1": 84.17, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "About 445 checks", "kicker": "2012 to 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.56, 0.83, 1.35, 1.72, 1.93, 2.23, 2.59, 2.67, 2.98, 4.06, 4.3]}, {"scene": "checks", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]", "links[4]"], "text": "More than 775,000 dollars.", "t0": 84.17, "t1": 86.73, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$775,000", "label": "from his own clients"}, "emph": ["More"], "wt": [0.04, 0.24, 0.42, 0.72, 1.07, 1.66, 2.02]}, {"scene": "hui", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[10]"], "text": "And the director, Tom Hui? He took meals from expediter Walter Wong and developer Zhang Li.", "t0": 87.35, "t1": 92.52, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Tom Hui", "kicker": "The director", "sub": "City Attorney report, March 10, 2020"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.22, 0.64, 0.98, 1.96, 2.13, 2.33, 2.61, 2.79, 3.3, 3.65, 4.03, 4.17, 4.62, 4.91]}, {"scene": "hui", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "That’s the City Attorney’s finding. Hui resigned the next day. He was never charged.", "t0": 92.64, "t1": 97.1, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Tom Hui", "kicker": "The director", "sub": "resigned March 11, 2020, never charged"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.35, 0.61, 1.03, 1.82, 2.08, 2.45, 2.53, 2.77, 3.32, 3.48, 3.63, 3.87]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[4]", "established[0]", "established[3]", "established[8]", "established[15]"], "text": "Santos got 30 months in prison. Curran, Pada and Yu, about a year each.", "t0": 97.32, "t1": 101.87, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The sentences", "sub": "Santos 30 months; Curran, Pada and Yu about a year each; Curran’s local perjury case: convicted September 29, 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.7, 0.99, 1.28, 1.37, 2.24, 2.72, 3.16, 3.33, 3.61, 3.83, 3.9, 4.15]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[6]", "established[9]"], "text": "The SIA executives got probation. So did Peter Schurman, for forging inspection reports.", "t0": 101.99, "t1": 107.0, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Probation", "sub": "the three SIA executives: a fine of $75,000 and two of $25,000; technician Peter Schurman, a $37,000 fine"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.64, 1.17, 1.38, 2.4, 2.62, 2.77, 3.01, 3.42, 3.59, 3.96, 4.45]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[5]", "established[4]", "established[13]"], "text": "Santos and partner Albert Urrutia settled the City’s lawsuit for 1.425 million dollars.", "t0": 107.12, "t1": 112.68, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "$1.425 million", "label": "civil settlement, June 3, 2025", "sub": "plus $113,818 to the City for the audit; Curran owes DBI $140,552.49"}, "emph": ["1.425 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.69, 1.08, 1.45, 1.95, 2.25, 2.35, 2.66, 3.1, 3.31, 3.55, 3.84, 4.12, 4.37, 4.67, 5.01]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[12]"], "text": "The City’s lawsuit went on against one property owner: a judgment, then an appeal in 2026.", "t0": 112.8, "t1": 117.87, "shot": "b24b", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The civil case goes on", "sub": "one property owner: judgment, then an appeal, February 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.43, 0.86, 1.08, 1.21, 1.56, 1.75, 2.17, 2.59, 2.75, 3.28, 3.5, 3.6, 3.97, 4.05, 4.38]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]"], "text": "No finding says which approved buildings, if any, were unsafe.", "t0": 117.99, "t1": 121.18, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Which approved buildings were unsafe", "Who lent Curran $260,000"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.69, 0.92, 1.1, 1.49, 1.99, 2.18, 2.42, 2.62]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[1]"], "text": "The department’s audit of Curran’s projects would show if approvals were reversed.", "t0": 121.3, "t1": 125.06, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "DBI’s audit of projects Curran inspected"}, {"who": "", "what": "Curran’s plea papers, which would name the lender"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.63, 0.97, 1.07, 1.45, 1.96, 2.14, 2.36, 2.49, 2.97, 3.13]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "timeline[16]"], "text": "All eight federal cases are closed.", "t0": 125.18, "t1": 127.08, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.51, 0.84, 1.22, 1.33]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.2, "t1": 129.43, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.69, 0.82, 1.1, 1.18, 1.26, 1.52, 1.79]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "char": "The charity · $9,600", "loan": "The loan · $260,000", "sia": "The plan checkers · 18 years", "checks": "The checks · $775,000", "hui": "The director", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "map", "hook": "number"}